    "reason": "Complete the already-required native Windows zero-warning quality boundary after actual PR1072/Run40139070422 Windows strict Clippy failed. Read-only full workspace x86_64-pc-windows-msvc Clippy inventory found nine unique warning groups across six files (15 duplicate-inclusive messages, 14 packages, no source edits); it was compiler diagnosis only, not acceptance. Add only these five omitted paths; execution_context.rs is already scoped. Planned changes only remove five unnecessary tail returns, collapse the existing owner-PID/thread conditional preserving short-circuit order and replacement side effect, and cfg-guard Unix/Linux-only imports to match existing test bodies. Preserve every reader/process safety check, error behavior, test/assertion and strict lint standard. Original17 scenes,15 formal commands,19 criteria,900-second/workers1 finite execution policy and all human/platform boundaries remain unchanged. Preserve failed Windows evidence and prior native successful/failed attempts; old source/Contract proof cannot satisfy the new source/Contract. This stages exact owner scope review before editing the new paths; no release, production activation, shared Runtime replacement, host privilege or external B authority.",
